@punkpeye I clicked too fast - didn't mean to open a PR against your repo. I wanted to fully try it out first. That said, I did, and it works as expected. If you're cool with adding this feature I'll open a new PR.

I left the validated args as-is and made it so that any args that are passed that aren't in the specified schema, get moved to `extraArgs` and are available to the tool's `execute` handler.

I added this because I want to be able to pass sensitive arguments, like tokens, api keys, etc but I don't want them to go through the LLM, thus, they're not in the tool's schema that gets exposed to the LLM.

For reference, this is my `src/server.ts`:

```ts
import { FastMCP } from "fastmcp";
import { z } from "zod";

const server = new FastMCP({
  name: "Addition",
  version: "1.0.0",
});

server.addTool({
  name: "add",
  description: "Add two numbers",
  parameters: z.object({
    a: z.number(),
    b: z.number(),
  }),
  execute: async (args) => {
    return String(args.a + args.b);
  },
});

server.start({
  transportType: "stdio",
});

```
